  body: |
    # Period for assessing ESA income other than self-employment

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source calls for the claim date, benefit-week start, due date, date treated as paid and payment period or stated alternative when deciding the period over which income is taken into account.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 48030 expressly excludes self-employment. Earnings on termination and exceptional payments have further provisions. The assessment period is an evidence question, not an automatic bank-receipt or calendar calculation.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 48030, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8020bded915d74e33f89b8/dmgch48.pdf#page=9)
    - [DMG 48031, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8020bded915d74e33f89b8/dmgch48.pdf#page=11)
    - [DMG 48048, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8020bded915d74e33f89b8/dmgch48.pdf#page=15)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:30.529917Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication, revision or commencement date. Source-stated dates retain their own role and precision.

